    {
      "path": "RESOURCE_BOUNDS.md",
      "line": 30,
      "kinds": [
        "request_response_deadline"
      ],
      "text": "ith_timeout_opt` on the client's clock) | `timeout`, 30 s by default (`default_timeout`), per client and replaceable per call: the transport's `send`, from the request to the whole buffered response. The default transport's own deadline is set to `Int` max (`transport_ceiling_ms`) so it never cuts a longer call timeout short | The exchange is cancelled and the call raises `RequestoError::Timeout` | `src/timing_test.mbt`: \"an exchange times out after 30 s on the client's clock by default\", \"timeout is set per client and replaced per call\"; `src/client_wbtest.mbt`: \"defaults: 30 s per exchange, 64 MiB per buffered body, a versioned User-Agent\" |",
      "excerpt_start_column": 67,
      "match_column": 227
    }
